***************************************************************** 2425 1451
    Covariances for Cr-50, S. Hoblit, BNL, Aug. 2011              2425 1451
                                                                  2425 1451
The COMMARA-2.0 covariances in the fast neutron region were       2425 1451
adopted for ENDF/B-VII.1. These covariances used the ENDF/B-VI.8  2425 1451
evaluation as the starting point. The reason was that both the    2425 1451
basic files (adopted by ENDF/B-VII.0) and covariances were        2425 1451
produced by the highly experience ORNL group, Hetrick etal (1991).2425 1451
We restored these covariances although CSEWG decided to drop them 2425 1451
from ENDF/B-VII.0. In case of Cr the justification for dropping   2425 1451
was relatively weak and mostly concerned the resonance region.    2425 1451
At inelastic scattering threshold region, the original            2425 1451
ENDF/B-VI.8 uncertainties were increased based on the dispersion  2425 1451
analysis of existing evaluations. Similarly, capture cross        2425 1451
sections uncertainties at high energies were increased to values  2425 1451
that were deemed to be more realistic.                            2425 1451
                                                                  2425 1451
An MF33 LB=5 section was added to the covariances for elastic     2425 1451
scattering at the upper end of the resonance region (2-783 keV)   2425 1451
to account for the uncertainty in the scattering radius R'. The   2425 1451
uncertainty in R' was taken from the Atlas of Neutron Resonances  2425 1451
and propagated to the elastic cross sections, using the 33-group  2425 1451
energy bins of the AFCI COMMARA-2.0 processed files. To account   2425 1451
for the capture uncertainty in COMMARA, an additional 5% MF33     2425 1451
LB=1 section was added from 100 - 783 keV, where long-range       2425 1451
correlations are not fully accounted for in MF32 alone.           2425 1451
                                                                  2425 1451
***************************************************************** 2425 1451
 24-Cr- 50 ORNL Resonance Evaluation Including Covariance         2425 1451
                                                                  2425 1451
 L. C. Leal, H. Derrien, K. Guber, G. Arbanas and D. Wiarda       2425 1451
                                                                  2425 1451
   Resolved resonance parameter evaluation for Cr-50 was done with2425 1451
the computer code SAMMY. Transmission measurements for highly     2425 1451
enriched samples of chromium isotopes, done by Harvey et al., were2425 1451
used in the evaluations.[1] One transmission measurement for Cr-502425 1451
done with a 95.98% enriched sample were used in the evaluation.   2425 1451
The transmission measurement was done at the Oak Ridge Electron   2425 1451
Linear Accelerator (ORELA) of the Oak Ridge National Laboratory.  2425 1451
The transmission data were measured at the 201-meter flight-path  2425 1451
in the energy range of 90-800 KeV. Thermal cross section data     2425 1451
available in the EXFOR data system were also included in the      2425 1451
evaluation.                                                       2425 1451
                                                                  2425 1451
   A set of resonance parameter describing the experimental data  2425 1451
was obtained. Resonance parameter covariance matrices were also   2425 1451
obtained in the SAMMY evaluation process. The Cr-50 evaluation was2425 1451
done in the energy region 10-5 eV 783 keV.[2]                     2425 1451
  Thermal cross section obtained in the present evaluation are    2425 1451
compared to the values listed in the Atlas of Neutron Resoances   2425 1451
in the following table:                                           2425 1451
                                                                  2425 1451
    Cross Section            ORNL                      Atlas      2425 1451
                                                                  2425 1451
       Capt               15.37+/-0.34              15.40+/-0.20  2425 1451
       Total              17.79+/-0.38                   -        2425 1451
       Scat                2.42+/-0.12                   -        2425 1451
                                                                  2425 1451
                    ORNL          ENDFBVII.0        JENDL4        2425 1451
      Res. Int  7.232+/-0.171      7.481             7.226        2425 1451
                                                         -        2425 1451
                                                                  2425 1451
