 **************************************************************** 2425 1451
                                                                  2425 1451
 ENDF/B-VI MOD 1 Evaluation, November 1989, D. Hetrick, D. Larson,2425 1451
                 N. Larson, C. Fu (ORNL)                          2425 1451
                                                                  2425 1451
   This work employed the Hauser-Feshbach code TNG [Fu88,Fu80,    2425 1451
 Si86].  The TNG code provides energy and angular distributions   2425 1451
 of particles emitted in the compound and pre-compound reactions, 2425 1451
 ensures consistency among all reactions, and maintains energy    2425 1451
 balance. Details pertinent to the contents of this evaluation    2425 1451
 will be published at a later date.                               2425 1451
                                                                  2425 1451
 Description of files ------------------------------------------- 2425 1451
 (MF-MT)                                                          2425 1451
  1-451 General information, references, and definitions.         2425 1451
  2-151 Resonance parameters;  used to provide the total,         2425 1451
        scattering, and capture cross sections from 1.E-5 eV to   2425 1451
        792 keV.  A small contribution in file 3-102 is added for 2425 1451
        capture from 325 to 792 keV (see 3-102 below). The        2425 1451
        resonance parameters are taken from Brusegan [Br85] with  2425 1451
        help from brusegan et al. (private comm., 1988), and are  2425 1451
        adjusted to give correct thermal values.  The parameters  2425 1451
        were also adjusted to the data of J.A. Harvey and H.M.    2425 1451
        Agrawal [Ha88], and a background file is given in 3-1 from2425 1451
        30 to 792 keV.  Note that the flag has been set to allow  2425 1451
        allow user calculation of the angular distributions from  2425 1451
        the R-Matrix resonance parameters, if the user wants      2425 1451
        angular distributions on a finer energy grid than given   2425 1451
        in 4-2.                                                   2425 1451
  3-1   Total cross section; given by resonance parameters up to  2425 1451
        792 keV with negative energy resonances adjusted to give  2425 1451
        measured thermal scattering and capture cross sections    2425 1451
        (see description for 3-102, below).  Above 792 keV,       2425 1451
        isotopic data used to 4.0 MeV [Ha88] and from 4.-20.0 MeV 2425 1451
        high resolution natural Cr transmission measurements were 2425 1451
        used, see Larson et al. [La88].                           2425 1451
  3-2   Elastic scattering cross section; obtained by subtracting 2425 1451
        the nonelastic from the total.                            2425 1451
  3-3   Nonelastic cross section; sum of 3-4, 3-16, 3-22,         2425 1451
        3-28, 3-102, 3-103, 3-104, and 3-107.                     2425 1451
  3-4   Total inelastic cross section; sum of 3-51, 3-52, ...     2425 1451
        ...,3-56, and 3-91                                        2425 1451
  3-16  (n,2n) cross section; taken from the measurements of      2425 1451
        Ghorai et al. [Gh87] and Ikeda et al. [Ik88].             2425 1451
  3-22  (n,na) cross section; calculated by the TNG code [Fu88,   2425 1451
        Fu80,Si86]; no data available other than a emission.      2425 1451
  3-28  (n,np) cross section; calculated by the TNG code [Fu88,   2425 1451
        Fu80,Si86].  Little data available; 3-28 added to 3-103   2425 1451
        agrees well with sparse p-emission data.                  2425 1451
  3-51 To 3-56 inelastic scattering exciting levels; results are  2425 1451
        from TNG [Fu88,Fu80,Si86].                                2425 1451
  3-91  Inelastic scattering exciting the continuum; TNG          2425 1451
        calculated.                                               2425 1451
  3-102 (n,g) capture cross section; given by resonance parameters2425 1451
        up to 792 keV and from 792 keV to 20 MeV, TNG calculations2425 1451
        were used but normalized to measured average capture      2425 1451
        between 100 keV and 792 keV.  A small contribution to be  2425 1451
        added to 2-151 is given from 325 to 792 keV due to        2425 1451
        incomplete experimental capture resonance information.    2425 1451
        TNG calculations included a precompound component and     2425 1451
        weighted cross sections from all isotopes of Cr give 0.82 2425 1451
        mb at 14.5 MeV, in agreement with the measurement of 0.75 2425 1451
        mb for natural Cr.                                        2425 1451
  3-103 (n,p) cross section; calculated by the TNG code [Fu88,    2425 1451
        Fu80,Si86].  Little data available; see 3-28 above.       2425 1451
  3-104 (n,d) cross section; shape of (n,p) cross section used;   2425 1451
        normalized to available data [Gr79].                      2425 1451
  3-107 (n,a) cross section; calculated by the TNG code [Fu88,    2425 1451
        Fu80,Si86].  3-22 added to 3-107 agrees well with sparse  2425 1451
        alpha-emission data.                                      2425 1451
  4-2   Angular distributions of secondary neutrons for elastic   2425 1451
        scattering; from ENDF/B-V.                                2425 1451
        If desired, angular distributions can be calculated by    2425 1451
        the user on a finer energy grid from the R-matrix         2425 1451
        resonance parameters in 2-151.                            2425 1451
  6-16  (n,2n) reaction; includes simple constant yields for the  2425 1451
        neutron and 49Cr residual, and energy dependent yield     2425 1451
        based on TNG calculated gamma-ray spectra for the gamma   2425 1451
        ray; TNG calculated normalized distributions are given for2425 1451
        each product.  Isotropy is assumed.                       2425 1451
  6-22  (n,na) reaction; includes simple constant yields for the  2425 1451
        neutron, alpha, and 46Ti residual, and energy dependent   2425 1451
        yield based on tng calculated gamma-ray spectra for the   2425 1451
        gamma ray; calculated normalized distributions are given  2425 1451
        for each product. Isotropy is assumed.                    2425 1451
  6-28  (n,np) reaction; includes simple constant yields for the  2425 1451
        neutron and 49V residual, and energy dependent yield      2425 1451
        based on TNG calculated gamma-ray spectra for the gamma   2425 1451
        ray; calculated normalized distributions are given for    2425 1451
        each product.  Isotropy is assumed.  (n,xp) d-d emission  2425 1451
        data used to benchmark the calculation.                   2425 1451
  6-51 through 6-56 inelastic scattering exciting levels;         2425 1451
        assumed isotropic.                                        2425 1451
  6-91  Inelastic scattering exciting the continuum; includes     2425 1451
        simple constant yields for the neutron and 50Cr residual  2425 1451
        and energy dependent yield based on TNG calculated        2425 1451
        gamma-ray spectra for the gamma ray; TNG calculated       2425 1451
        normalized distributions are given for each.  Isotropy    2425 1451
        is assumed.                                               2425 1451
  6-103 (n,p) reaction; includes simple constant yields for p     2425 1451
        and 50V residual, and energy dependent yield based        2425 1451
        on calculated gamma-ray spectra for gamma ray;            2425 1451
        calculated normalized distributions are given for each    2425 1451
        product.  Isotropy is assumed.  (n,xp) d-d emission data  2425 1451
        used to benchmark the calculation.                        2425 1451
  6-107 (n,a) reaction; includes simple constant yields for alpha 2425 1451
        and 47Ti residual, and energy dependent yield based       2425 1451
        on calculated gamma-ray spectra for gamma ray; calculated 2425 1451
        normalized distributions are given for each product.      2425 1451
        Isotropy is assumed.  (n,xa) d-d emission data used to    2425 1451
        benchmark the calculation.                                2425 1451
 12-51 through 12-56 branching ratios for the levels are given.   2425 1451
 12-102 (n,g) capture;  TNG calculated.                           2425 1451
 14-51 through 14-56 and 14-102 gamma ray angular distributions;  2425 1451
        assumed to be isotropic.                                  2425 1451
 15-102 (n,g) capture;  TNG calculated.                           2425 1451
                                                                  2425 1451
 ---------------------------------------------------------------- 2425 1451
 Uncertainty files                                                2425 1451
    An LB=8 section is included for all non-derived files as      2425 1451
        required by ENDF/B-VI.                                    2425 1451
                                                                  2425 1451
 33-1   Uncertainties are derived from 1.E-5 to 100 eV.  From 100 2425 1451
        eV to 20 MeV they are explicit, using LB=0,1 and 8.       2425 1451
 33-2   From 1.E-5 to 100 eV, uncertainties are explicit, based   2425 1451
        upon thermal uncertainty and other data.  From 100 eV to  2425 1451
        20 MeV the files are derived.                             2425 1451
 33-3   From 1.E-5 to 792 keV uncertainties are derived.  From    2425 1451
        792 keV to 20 MeV uncertainties are explicit, using LB=1  2425 1451
        and 8.                                                    2425 1451
 33-4   Uncertainties are all derived.                            2425 1451
 33-16  Uncertainties for (n,2n) are explicit, estimated from TNG.2425 1451
 33-22  Uncertainties for (n,na) are explicit, estimated from TNG.2425 1451
 33-28  Uncertainties for (n,np) are explicit, estimated from TNG.2425 1451
 33-51 through 3-91  Uncertainties for inelastic scattering are   2425 1451
        explicit, based on data and calculation uncertainties.    2425 1451
 33-102 Uncertainties are explicit, based on thermal data at low  2425 1451
        energies, and calculated results above 792 keV.           2425 1451
 33-104 Uncertainties estimated, based on data.                   2425 1451
 33-103 Uncertainties estimated from TNG.                         2425 1451
 33-107 Uncertainties estimated from TNG.                         2425 1451
